        <div class="main">
            <div class="project-intro typewriter">
                <div class="project-intro-inner">
                    <h1 class="project-title" data-chars="1" data-speed="50">New Junction</h1>
                    <hr>
                    <div class="project-details-wrapper">
                        <div class="project-details">
                            <h2>Client</h2>
                            <p>City of Swan</p>

                            <h2>Involvement</h2>
                            <p>Brand Identity</p>
                            <p>Brand Guidelines</p>
                            <p>Brand Implementation </p>
                            <p>Signage</p>
                            <p>Digital Communications</p>
                            <p>Video Production</p>
                            <p>Website Design</p>
                            <p>Print Templates</p>

                            <div class="awards">
                                <h2>Recognition</h2>
                                <p><a href="https://agda.com.au/awards/results/4462/" target="_blank">AGDA Awards 2018 Merit — Identity&nbsp;Manuals</a></p>
                                <div class="awards-logos wait-for-typewriter">
                                    <img alt="AGDA Award" title="AGDA Award" src="/assets/award-agda.svg">
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="project-description">
                            <h2>Challenge</h2>
                            <p>The town of Midland in WA has long been a meeting place of people from dozens of countries and diverse backgrounds. It’s a town that’s been built on hard work and determination – on heavy industry and agriculture.</p>
                            <p>Midland’s seldom used oval laying at its heart was primed for transformation into a new meeting place that would become the town’s new backyard. An area that would create spaces for new trees and wildlife – along with homes, offices, restaurants, cafés and bars. The town required a brand that could bring this vision to life.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="project-description">
                            <h2>Solution</h2>
                            <p>The New Junction brand reflects the heritage of Midland, and injects that same new life and energy into the visuals. Using vibrant and nostalgic imagery, typography and textures derived from Midland’s backyard, the brand tells the story of Midland’s history through the lens of the people who built it.</p>
                            <p>A fresh and energetic colour palette inspired by classic Australian imagery has been created – pulling colours from old milk bars, cricket and football posters, signage, cereal boxes and much more. A flexible typographic system allows for a vibrant expression of messages through a nostalgic voice.</p>
                            <!-- <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDKGsLQ0vCQ" target="_blank" class="button after-arrow wait-for-typewriter">Watch the video</a> -->
                            <p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDKGsLQ0vCQ" target="_blank" class="dotted after-arrow">Watch the video</a></p>
                            <div class="collab-logos wait-for-typewriter">
                                <img alt="Cameron Murray" title="Cameron Murray" src="/assets/logo-cameron-murray.svg">
                                <img alt="Block Branding" title="Block Branding" src="/assets/logo-block.svg">
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
